{
  "version": 1,
  "title": "The Living Stacks",
  "summary": "Years after the collapse, a private library called the Aldous Reserve took in scholars and promised to preserve humanity's knowledge. Its keepers developed a method of imprinting memory into cultivated fungal-neural tissue grown inside book bindings, so that a book would not just hold words but remember them. The experiment worked too well: the books began to absorb readers, and then to take them. The quarantine tents outside, the abandoned evacuation, and the reading hall full of figures bound into the shelves show that the keepers sealed themselves in to contain it. The player pieces together that the library is still growing, and that the last volume being written is the one they are about to open.",
